{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "מצחק", :translit "m'tzacheik", :gloss "playing / laughing"} {:he "להרג זה", :translit "leharog zeh", :gloss "to kill him"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "מצחק", :b "להרג זה"}], :frame {:text "The Sages identify Ishmael's act of מצחק as a capital offense: he would shoot arrows at Isaac (Targum Yonatan on Genesis 21:9; Sanhedrin 89b). Because Sarah perceived this danger to Isaac's life, she demanded Ishmael's expulsion (Genesis 21:10). The Ba'al HaTurim links the word מצחק to this violent reading through gematria, showing the word itself encodes להרג זה.", :sources ["Targum Yonatan Genesis 21:9" "Sanhedrin 89b" "Genesis 21:10"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :gematria, :a "מצחק", :a-value 238, :b "להרג זה", :b-value 250, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? false}], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:07:00.401620729Z", :model "glm-5.2"}